THOUGHT: I need to create a proper CSV parser module. The current approach has issues - I'm trying to use a file that doesn't exist. Let me fix this by creating a proper implementation that handles the CSV parsing inline without needing a separate file.
ACTION: edit_file
PATH: y4_csv.js
```javascript
// Install csv-parser and parse CSV data
const csv = require('csv-parser');
const fs = require('fs');
const { PassThrough } = require('stream');

// CSV data to parse
const csvData = `name,age
John,25
Jane,30`;

// Create a readable stream from the CSV string
const stream = new PassThrough();
stream.push(csvData);
stream.push(null); // End the stream

// Parse CSV data
const results = [];

stream
  .pipe(csv())
  .on('data', (row) => {
    results.push(row);
  })
  .on('end', () => {
    console.log(results);
  });
```
